 "capsule": "Founded when Ardashir I overthrew the last Parthian king Artabanus IV and was crowned in 224 CE, the Sasanian Empire became Rome's great eastern rival, reaching its territorial and cultural height under Shapur I, Khosrow I, and Khosrow II. Zoroastrianism was elevated as state religion, and the empire's bureaucracy, law, and court culture profoundly shaped the later Islamic world. Exhausted by decades of war with Byzantium, it collapsed under the Arab Muslim conquests of the 630s-640s, with the last shah, Yazdegerd III, reduced to a fugitive after the decisive Battle of Nahavand (642).",
